# wastelands-bart - machine-readable palette
#
# HAND-CONFIGURED by tricolor.py. Do NOT regenerate with
# `palette.py build` - that emits the fixed two-axis seam and
# would silently discard the layout below.
#
# ground 105, leaf 94, accent 262, detail 262, saturation 1.45.
#
# Source: wildflower-field wallpaper (Screenshot 2026-08-31 at 14-46-55.png),
# a golden-yellow bloom field under a blue sky. Two-color duo:
#   MAJOR  the field   - backgrounds, near-neutral text ramp, accent_vivid
#   SECOND the sky     - border, cursor, accent family, text_muted/dim, reserves
#
# The sky measured 9.9% chroma-weighted share, 0.1% under the 10% floor,
# and was kept anyway: it covers 14.5% of pixels at median chroma 0.064,
# a coherent region rather than noise, and moving all visible chrome onto
# blue (hue 262, in the wide blue gap: 79 deg from teal, 43 from mauve) is
# what keeps the accent family clear of warning-yellow. A one-color build
# at the measured hue 94 would have parked every accent 8 deg from yellow.
#
# Hue shifts:
#   ground 94 -> 105  to widen clearance from yellow (86.5) for the
#                     chroma-boosted dark roles; the image's own green
#                     patches at 117 keep this honest.
#   leaf stays 94     the text ramp is low-chroma, judged by dE not hue,
#                     and keeps the field's golden cast.
#
# Saturation 1.45: image median chroma is 0.091 (1.78x goa-cove) but that
# is dominated by the field; the sky axis measures 0.064 (1.25x). 1.45
# splits the difference. At 1.78 the collision resolver had to drag text
# down to L 0.804; at 1.45 it lands at 0.828 (#D4C6A0, 9.68:1), a warm
# parchment accepted deliberately - a pale warm ramp is inherently near
# catppuccin yellow, and it stays under the 60% saturation guard.
#
# Provenance (palette.py check --image): SAMPLED - bg_raised, bg_selection,
# text_muted, text_dim, accent_bright, accent_vivid. Everything else is
# EXTRAPOLATED: the image's darkest chromatic pixels sit near L 0.39 so the
# bg pair is extrapolated downward, and the whole image tops out at L 0.833
# so text_bright (needs 0.967) and the upper text ramp are invented.
#
# Advisory warnings accepted: text/text_secondary/text_hint/accent_vivid sit
# 4-13 deg from yellow by hue, but all clear the binding dE-plus-saturation
# gate; accent_bright is dE 0.032 from syntax blue (advisory, matches the
# 0.023-0.05 range every palette here lands in).

[background]
bg=#202101
bg_surface=#2E2D03
bg_raised=#423F1B
bg_selection=#54530B

[text]
text_bright=#F8F4E7
text=#D4C6A0
text_secondary=#BAB191
text_muted=#85A1DE
text_dim=#5E8AD2
text_hint=#9E9575

[chrome]
border=#4576CD
cursor=#ADD1FD
accent=#5780F6
accent_bright=#87B2E4
accent_light=#83B0EA
accent_soft=#84A0F3
accent_vivid=#C0AA27

[reserve]
reserve_1=#7FADFA
reserve_2=#6C9DF9
reserve_3=#608DF8
reserve_4=#204BA8
